  data: {
    LLM: 'Avoid winning early tricks if possible. Sluff (discard) low-to-mid range cards early to preserve high cards (Aces, 10s) for the final trick. If you must win, do so with the lowest possible card.\n\nThe 3 Strategy: The 3 is the weakest card but carries a multiplier bonus in Cameroon variant. Winning the final trick with a 3 is more valuable than with higher cards because of the stake multiplier, though it requires precise control of previous tricks.\n\nSuit Tracking: Memorize which high cards (particularly Aces and 10s) have been played in each suit. Position yourself to lead the final trick with a card that others cannot beat with their remaining cards. Force opponents into wasteful high-card plays early by leading their strong suits.',
    Player: 'Avoid winning early tricks if possible. Sluff (discard) low-to-mid range cards early to preserve high cards (Aces, 10s) for the final trick. If you must win, do so with the lowest possible card.\n\nThe 3 Strategy: The 3 is the weakest card but carries a multiplier bonus in Cameroon variant. Winning the final trick with a 3 is more valuable than with higher cards because of the stake multiplier, though it requires precise control of previous tricks.\n\nSuit Tracking: Memorize which high cards (particularly Aces and 10s) have been played in each suit. Position yourself to lead the final trick with a card that others cannot beat with their remaining cards. Force opponents into wasteful high-card plays early by leading their strong suits.',
